WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.072 --> 00:00:04.720
Speaker 1: Let's follow up about school lunch.&nbsp;
This story is just vile. We've talked about&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.720 --> 00:00:11.120
Republicans and school lunch before. The&nbsp;
news is that Mitch McConnell is reportedly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:11.120 --> 00:00:18.640
again opposing free school lunch. The Washington&nbsp;
Post reports that Mitch McConnell is opposing an&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:18.640 --> 00:00:24.080
extension to the free school lunch program. This&nbsp;
comes as Congress is deciding what to include in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:24.080 --> 00:00:31.920
the upcoming government funding package. You may&nbsp;
recall that again, we are in the situation where&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:31.920 --> 00:00:37.440
the Free School Lunch, the Comprehensive Free&nbsp;
School Lunch program that was started and expanded&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:37.440 --> 00:00:44.560
during the pandemic, has an expiration date&nbsp;
on it. And now there are Republican lawmakers,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:44.560 --> 00:00:51.920
including Mitch McConnell, who oppose including&nbsp;
that in a new government funding package.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:53.280 --> 00:00:59.440
I have to tell you that this is one of the most&nbsp;
vile things like you really have to understand&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:00.080 --> 00:01:05.840
the degree to which these people cannot empathize&nbsp;
with anybody else. And we've talked about&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:05.840 --> 00:01:11.680
opposition to free school lunch from the right&nbsp;
wing before. Remember this clip from October,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:11.680 --> 00:01:17.920
where Fox News anchor Martha MacCallum is like,&nbsp;
Listen, if kids think school lunch is free, then&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:18.560 --> 00:01:21.440
I guess something very bad would happen.
Speaker 2: One of the things that kills me&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:21.440 --> 00:01:25.840
is that now that you know, there's a free lunch&nbsp;
program in New Jersey and it's for everyone,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:25.840 --> 00:01:30.160
even if you you don't need help to send your&nbsp;
child's lunch to school. So those kids are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:30.160 --> 00:01:34.640
all going to grow up thinking what school is for&nbsp;
lunch is free, right? And then God help the person&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:34.640 --> 00:01:39.120
who comes along and tries to take that away.
Speaker 1: Like these kids might grow up thinking&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:39.120 --> 00:01:46.800
school lunch is free. And why shouldn't it be?&nbsp;
Why shouldn't it be in a literal sense? Of course,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:46.800 --> 00:01:52.800
food's not free. You understand this. I understand&nbsp;
this. It's, you know, people pay property taxes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:52.800 --> 00:01:59.120
and it funds schools and you're paying for&nbsp;
school lunch. Sometimes property taxes include&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:59.120 --> 00:02:05.120
trash pick up. The trash pickup isn't literally&nbsp;
free. It's paid for through your property tax.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:05.120 --> 00:02:14.000
OK. Sometimes. It's good when we pay for things&nbsp;
with taxes, and sometimes it's not so good. So,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:14.000 --> 00:02:20.080
for example, many of us would say, I don't love&nbsp;
that my taxes without any option. I mean, OK,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:20.080 --> 00:02:24.880
you know, we could replace everybody to and&nbsp;
the military industrial complex and only elect&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:24.880 --> 00:02:28.640
people who won't support it in any way. It's not&nbsp;
realistic that that's going to happen overnight.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:28.640 --> 00:02:32.800
I don't necessarily love tax money going to some&nbsp;
of the weapons that it goes towards. OK, fine.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:32.800 --> 00:02:40.080
When we're talking about school lunch, first&nbsp;
of all, it's so cheap. It's so cheap. Secondly,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:40.080 --> 00:02:46.160
it's really stigmatizing. A lot of schools still&nbsp;
have this colored lunch ticket program at my&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:46.160 --> 00:02:53.680
elementary school. You know, 90 years ago, if you&nbsp;
paid full price for lunch, you got a green ticket.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:54.320 --> 00:03:01.120
And if you got the discounted lunch, you got a&nbsp;
yellow ticket. And if you got free lunch, you had&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:01.120 --> 00:03:06.960
I think it was like a red ticket or whatever.&nbsp;
It's extraordinarily stigmatizing to do that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:06.960 --> 00:03:13.120
in elementary schools in a way that can be really&nbsp;
damaging to kids. And when they say, you know, we&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:13.120 --> 00:03:18.480
can't have kids growing up thinking that it's&nbsp;
free if property taxes cover school lunch,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:19.280 --> 00:03:23.520
what's the big, devastating realization&nbsp;
that kids will come to? It's just,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:23.520 --> 00:03:29.200
oh, the lunch is free. We pay for it through&nbsp;
property taxes. All right. Well, I understand it.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:29.200 --> 00:03:35.040
School is mandatory. You have to be there, but&nbsp;
they don't have to give you food at no additional&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:35.040 --> 00:03:39.920
cost. At the point of purchase, you have to&nbsp;
be there and your property taxes pay for it.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:39.920 --> 00:03:46.160
There are kids, depending on the school lunch, in&nbsp;
order to eat. And Republicans don't want to do it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:46.160 --> 00:03:49.520
either because they say we can't afford it&nbsp;
because we obviously can, or because they&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:49.520 --> 00:03:55.440
think that children are going to be taught some&nbsp;
bad lesson. Is it a good thing to be thinking that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:56.800 --> 00:04:03.600
if you're a kid in school to be thinking that&nbsp;
whether I eat depends on anything other than just,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:03.600 --> 00:04:08.400
am I here? Can my parents afford it or not? Did&nbsp;
Mitch McConnell extend the program or not? Or&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:08.400 --> 00:04:13.440
will you get lunch and you don't? It's absurd.&nbsp;
It's absurd. And of course, it's not even really&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:13.440 --> 00:04:18.160
free. It's just prepaid. That's really all that&nbsp;
we're talking about. And when you step back,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:18.880 --> 00:04:23.920
if you are a politician and you think&nbsp;
so-called free school lunch is a problem,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:24.880 --> 00:04:30.480
then you're not even in the right universe. You're&nbsp;
not even in the right galaxy when thinking about&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:30.480 --> 00:04:35.520
the problems that we have. And Mitch McConnell now&nbsp;
joining the train in saying, No, no, no, no, no.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:35.520 --> 00:04:40.320
We can't allow this to happen. School lunch&nbsp;
should just be free period and by free, I mean,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:40.320 --> 00:04:46.880
prepaid through property taxes as it already is,&nbsp;
but for everybody rather than just some people.

